'''azan''' (a-zän′), ''n.'' [Ar.] In Mohammedan countries, the call to public prayers, proclaimed by the crier from the minaret of the mosque.

{{smaller block|When their crier, a small wizen-faced man, began the ''Azan'', we received it with a shout of derision, and some, hastily snatching up their weapons, offered him an opportunity of martyrdom.
{{right|''R. F. Burton'', El-Medinah, p. 133.}}}}

'''azarin''' (az′a-rin), ''n.'' A coal-tar color of the azo-group used in dyeing. {{smaller|It is applied only to cotton, and is fairly fast to light. It is a compound of naph-}}

